avformat/mov: read WebVTT subtitles stored in ISOBMFF ('wvtt')

ISO/IEC 14496-30 stores WebVTT in MP4 as a 'wvtt' sample entry whose samples
are boxes: a 'vttc' for each cue shown during the sample, with the text in
'payl' and an optional identifier ('iden') and settings ('sttg'), or a 'vtte'
for a stretch without cues. DASH and CMAF streams carry their subtitles this
way. The demuxer had no mapping for the entry, so the stream stayed a data
stream with no codec and players listed no subtitle track for it.

Map 'wvtt' to the WebVTT codec and turn each sample into a WebVTT packet: the
texts of its cues joined by line breaks, with the first cue's identifier and
settings as side data, as the Matroska and WebVTT demuxers give them. Samples
without cues are dropped once their timing has been accounted for.

--- a/libavformat/mov.c
+++ b/libavformat/mov.c
@@ -2801,6 +2801,9 @@
                 id = (format == MOV_MP4_TTML_TAG || format == MOV_ISMV_TTML_TAG) ?
                      AV_CODEC_ID_TTML : id;
             }
+            /* ISO/IEC 14496-30 WebVTT; get_wvtt_packet() turns its samples into WebVTT packets. */
+            if (id <= 0 && format == MKTAG('w','v','t','t'))
+                id = AV_CODEC_ID_WEBVTT;
 
             if (id > 0)
                 st->codecpar->codec_type = AVMEDIA_TYPE_SUBTITLE;
@@ -11600,6 +11603,114 @@
